.TH DISKMOON 1 "2026-06-19" "diskmoon 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diskmoon \- show where the disk space went, what can be freed and what nobody can see
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskmoon
.RI [ options ] " " [ path ]
.br
.B diskmoon
.RI [ options ] " " \-f " " FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diskmoon
scans a directory tree in parallel and explains its disk usage.
In a terminal it opens an interactive view; when the output is a pipe or a file,
or with
.B \-o
or
.BR \-F ,
it writes the complete report instead.
The path defaults to
.IR / .
.PP
Sizes are the space allocated on disk, with hard links counted once, so the totals
match
.BR "du \-sxB1" .
Disk sizes, used and free space match
.BR "df \-B1" .
.PP
Besides the tree, the report explains the space that no visible path holds
(deleted files still open by programs, files hidden under mount points, the
reserve for root, filesystem overhead), lists caches and build output that are
safe to delete together with the official command to clean each one, and can
compare the scan with an earlier one.
.PP
.B diskmoon
only reads. It never deletes anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write to
.I FILE
.RB ( \- " for standard output)."
A name ending in
.I .json
or
.I .csv
picks the format.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-format " " \fIFMT\fR
.I txt
(the report),
.I ncdu
(ncdu JSON export) or
.IR csv .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-from " " \fIFILE\fR
Read an ncdu JSON export instead of scanning
.RB ( \- " for standard input)."
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-save [ =\fIFILE\fR ]
Also keep this scan as ncdu JSON, by default in the scan history.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compare " " \fIFILE\fR
Show what grew, shrank, appeared or went away since an older scan.
.I last
means the newest scan of the same path in the history.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-depth " " \fIN\fR
Show the tree down to depth
.IR N .
Sizes stay complete.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-min\-size " " \fISIZE\fR
Fold entries smaller than
.I SIZE
(for example 10M or 1G).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-top " " \fIN\fR
List the
.I N
largest files (default 50).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Scanner threads.
The default is the number of CPUs up to 32, or 2 on a spinning disk.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-one\-file\-system
Stay on the filesystem of the starting path.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-apparent\-size
Count the file length instead of the allocated blocks.
.TP
.BR \-\-duplicates [ =\fISIZE\fR ]
Also find files with the same content, from
.I SIZE
up (default 1M).
Files are grouped by size, then by a hash of the first 64K, then by a hash of
the whole content.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-fs
Also enter tmpfs, proc, fuse and other mounts that are not disks.
.TP
.B \-\-dirs\-only
Hide files in the tree. They still count in the totals.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Draw the tree with ASCII characters.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No progress on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH INTERACTIVE VIEW
.TP
.BR 1 " " 2 " " 3 " " 4 ", " Tab
Switch between Report, Files, Free and Changes.
.TP
.BR Up " " Down ", " j " " k
Move. Page Up, Page Down, Home and End jump further.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Right
Open the folder. In Free, show the item in Files.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Backspace
Back to the parent folder.
.TP
.B /
In Files, filter the folder by name. In the other tabs, find text;
.B n
goes to the next match.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the filter, or stop a folder that is still being read.
.TP
.B s
In Files, sort by size, name, last change or item count.
.TP
.B w
Write the full report to a .txt file in the current folder.
.TP
.B S
Save this scan, so the Changes tab can compare against it next time.
.TP
.B ?
Show every key.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH REPORT
.TP
.B SUMMARY
How full the disk is, the heaviest spot and how much can be freed, in plain words.
.TP
.B WHAT YOU CAN FREE
Caches, build output and other known leftovers.
Each finding is marked
.I safe
or
.I check
and comes with the command to clean it and the space it frees.
.TP
.B FILESYSTEMS " and " CAPACITY
Every disk the scan touched: size, used, free, what the scan found, and how the
device size splits into filesystem overhead, the reserve for root and the space
for users.
.TP
.B NOT SEEN
Space counted as used that no visible path holds, broken down by cause.
.TP
.B BY FILE TYPE ", " UNTOUCHED ", " DUPLICATE FILES
Space by extension, folders unchanged for more than a year, and copies of the
same content
.RB ( \-\-duplicates ).
.TP
.B LARGEST FILES " and " TREE
The biggest files, and every folder with its share of the parent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/diskmoon/scans/
Scan history used by
.B \-\-save
and
.BR "\-\-compare last" .
Without
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
.I ~/.local/share/diskmoon/scans/
is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, even when some paths could not be read (they are listed in the report).
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments, a path or file that cannot be opened, or an output that cannot be written.
.TP
.B 2
Out of memory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo diskmoon
Open the interactive view on the whole system.
.TP
.B diskmoon \-o report.txt ~
Write the report of the home folder.
.TP
.B diskmoon \-s ~ && diskmoon \-c last ~
Save a scan, and later see what changed since then.
.TP
.B diskmoon \-o tree.json /srv && diskmoon \-f tree.json
Export a scan and open it again without touching the disk.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR ncdu (1)
